"""Native carriageway sweeps between the live junction mouths.

One metadata point describes one complete, ordered Section.  The node group
samples and validates the *actual* source mesh, filters collinear samples from
its temporary curve, replaces attached endpoints by mouth positions, rounds
interior polyline corners, then sweeps a direct quad Grid.  It never makes
triangles or copies a surface prepared by Python.

The planar path uses native circular-arc Bezier fillets.  At each interior vertex
with turning angle a, the cut-back is r*tan(a/2).  We allow at most 45% of either
adjacent trimmed leg, so neighboring fillets cannot consume the same leg.  The
requested radius is 1.5*width and the minimum accepted radius is width+2*abs(offset).
That minimum leaves the inner pavement radius at least half the center radius;
short/sharp bends are rejected instead of silently making inverted quads.

Sampling is uniform in centerline arc length.  The transverse parameter is
u=0..1 with 2*Radial Samples*2**(resolution-1) intervals.  The crown is
z=datum+exaggeration*rise*4*u*(1-u), retaining the full input profile at both mouths.
Mouth positions and tangents are forced exactly at the first/last sample row.
"""
